  "notes": "{苛立|いらだ}つ expresses a feeling of irritation or frustration.\n\nVERB TYPE:\n- Godan verb (つ-verb)\n- Intransitive\n\nWRITING:\n- {苛|いら} means \"harsh, cruel\" but here expresses irritation\n- Often written in hiragana: いらだつ, いら{立|だ}つ\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {苛立|いらだ}った{声|こえ} (irritated voice)\n- {苛立|いらだ}った{様子|ようす} (irritated manner)\n- {苛立|いらだ}ちを{感|かん}じる (to feel irritation)\n- {苛立|いらだ}ちを{隠|かく}せない (unable to hide irritation)\n\nFORMS:\n- {苛立|いらだ}ち (noun: irritation, frustration)\n- {苛立|いらだ}たしい (adjective: irritating)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- イライラする (to be irritated - onomatopoeia, more casual)\n- {腹|はら}が{立|た}つ (to get angry - stronger)\n- じれったい (frustrating - focus on impatience)\n- {焦|あせ}る (to be impatient)\n\nUSAGE:\n- Stronger than simple annoyance\n- Often visible in behavior or tone\n- Can be caused by waiting, inconvenience, or frustrating situations\n\nREGISTER: Neutral. Common in everyday conversation.",
